# Billing — Dev clock (non-production only)
# UC-138: move the clock Billing date rules read. Registered only when APP_ENV is local or staging
# (404 in production). The offset lives in the process: on staging hold the backend to ONE instance
# while the clock is in use (docs/RUNBOOKS.md § Billing). Compare `instanceId` across calls.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl     = {{backendUrl}}
@internalKey = {{$dotenv INTERNAL_API_KEY}}

### Current offset and the instance that answered
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/clock
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

###

### Move the clock forward 1 day + 2 hours (26 h). Non-negative integers, total > 0.
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/clock/advance
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "days": 1, "hours": 2 }

###

### Invalid: fractional / negative / empty → 400 GENERIC_VALUE_OUT_OF_RANGE
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/clock/advance
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "days": 1.5 }

###

### Back to real time (idempotent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/clock/reset
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
